   "golden": "\"Lives in water\" is not a feature for a key, and neither is \"is big\" or \"is brown\". A key must work on the specimen in front of you, whatever its age and whether or not you know where it was found. Ask only what you can see: the number of legs, wings or none, scales or feathers, a leaf edge smooth or toothed.",
